# cmdline.txt is a single line — do not append this as a new line.
# Verify the real path first (see deploy/README.md — /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt on
# recent Raspberry Pi OS, /boot/cmdline.txt on older).
#
# Insert the following token into the existing line, immediately after "rootwait",
# separated by a single space from its neighbors on both sides:
#
#   modules-load=dwc2
#
# Just dwc2 -- the usb0 network interface itself is created by
# nannycam-usb-gadget.service (a configfs-based CDC-NCM gadget) at boot,
# not by a modules-load=dwc2,g_ether legacy gadget module. See
# ncm-gadget.sh and deploy/README.md for why (Windows driver compatibility).
#
# Example — if the existing line reads:
#   console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=xxxxxxxx-02 rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait
# it should become:
#   console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=xxxxxxxx-02 rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait modules-load=dwc2
#
# A stray newline anywhere in this file will stop the Pi from booting.
